WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.793
Settings now tunes how the 3D world is drawn, so the ride stays smooth on the device

00:00:07.793 --> 00:00:09.086
beside the bike.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.648
Quality comes as five cards. Auto is chosen and recommended: it starts at Low and

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:18.052
steps down whenever frames drop.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.195
Pick a fixed level, and stepping down becomes yours to turn off. Frame rate,

00:00:28.195 --> 00:00:31.240
resolution and the graphics API sit below.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:41.275
The world follows. A race opens at the level chosen, draws at most thirty frames a

00:00:41.275 --> 00:00:44.711
second when asked, and scales only its own pixels.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:51.899
The World section, from a phone to the full screen.

00:00:59.361 --> 00:01:04.947
Without WebGPU, Ultra waits for it. Without 3D at all, Settings says so, and every

00:01:04.947 --> 00:01:06.610
World control rests.

00:01:09.685 --> 00:01:14.288
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:14.633 --> 00:01:19.145
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:20.816
every hill and interval.

00:01:21.161 --> 00:01:26.339
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:26.339 --> 00:01:31.787
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:31.787 --> 00:01:34.777
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:35.123 --> 00:01:37.615
A custom workout lives under Profile.
